A||||10||Philphine||any runners?||||1||
Z||000000||Philphine||11-15-2000||11:21 AM||||<BR>if you live somewhere that has cold winters what do you do? wrap up and get your miles in or find a gym? some kind of home equipment? i'm not a serious runner but i'd like to try to stay in some kind of shape over the winter and i hate running in the cold. don't really like other types of exercise but as i get older it's hard to just jump back out there in the spring and pick up where i left off.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||11-15-2000||11:35 AM||||I play soccer (which unfortunately is a winter sport) every saturday. Imagine running around in shorts and shirt, raining and temperatures near freezing point. Yeah - it's a great sport...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||11-15-2000||12:45 PM||||The company where I work has an indoor fitness center.  Every other day, I run about an hour on a treadmill.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SpeedPhreak||11-15-2000||05:37 PM||||soccer?  come on cliff.. RUGBY.  now thats a sport  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  my favorite ive ever played.<P>as far as your run.. well i say get some tight spandex pants.. yuck.  some light gloves & a light hat & go run.  after a 1/2 mile or so u should be producing enough heat to keep you warm.  or u could just ski/snowboard everyday  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||gixxer||11-15-2000||06:25 PM||||Ran from a cop once! <BR>Potential jaywalking ticket..<BR>Fight or flight instincts I guess.||||reg||1
Z||000005||william_thorniii||11-15-2000||06:27 PM||||Phillipine,<P>Running in the winter isn't as bad as you might think.  The worst part is how sore your ears get.  No the worst part is how cold you are during warm up.  No, I was wrong, the worst part is during cool down your muscles cool much faster than they are supposed to because of the temperature.  Nevermind, I am going to go with the ears/headache thing.  <P>Maybe running in the winter sucks.  <P>j/k once you get going, the cold air feels good (except for the cold ear/headache thing really).  <P>Cliff,<P>I played soccer on a traveling team for many years growing up.  I almost got an opportunity to travel abroad for a season... but didn't work out.  When the weather starts to turn cold here I always say "I feel like playing football today".  Most of my friends think I am nuts for wanting to take most of my clothes off in the freezing weather... but it is something about those cold and rainy games that I just love.  Hmmm is it how hard the ball feels when it hits you in the head beyond mid field when punted from the keeper, or is it how wet and muddy all of your clothes are when you try to get into your Fiero w/o ruining the interior.  Maybe I don't like the cold and wet games... :~)<P>I think rugby is awesome... but not too many places to play here in Ohio. <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000006||Uaana||11-15-2000||07:21 PM||||I think it depends on your def of cold. I myself hate running in under 70f temps. But living up here I do warm ups inside then go outside I give up after 32f and just use a bike at the local club.||||reg||1
Z||000007||RossT||11-15-2000||11:33 PM||||I run year round.  In fact I run more in the winter, because the snow helps cusion the constant pounding.  The key is to layer with quality garment.  When its below zero, I wear<BR>3 thin layers on top and bottom. a good ski mask helps to. Gortex is the best stuff ever made!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||2xsess||11-16-2000||07:24 AM||||Phil, as the Army says, "suck it up and drive on" J/K<P>We wear shorts,t-shirt with sweats over top for when it's mildly cold, then when it gets cold cold we add a watch cap and gloves. The watchcap helps stop the cold ear thing.lol<BR>It always seems to help when we do some warm-ups like sit-ups and pushups to get the blood flowing.<P>Good Luck.<BR>Jeff||||reg||1
Z||000009||Philphine||11-16-2000||12:31 PM||||when i'm at my most commited i try to get a run in if it's at least 40 deg ( only 40? ...yes i'm wimpy) but i hate it. perfect for me is about 50-60deg.<P>the area i'm in determines my route so right now it's every other day 4 mls and the day that falls on a weekend day 9mls.<P>i want to stay with it 'cause the 3 main local runs are in the spring and since i'm just starting again i never do as well as i could if they were happenning about now.<P>imma try to do better this winter though. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||RiceCooker||11-16-2000||02:02 PM||||Come, on! How cold could it possibly be in Kentucky? <BR>Way up here in the great white north, I have to put on my parka and my snowshoes when i leave my igloo to try and go running. But my snot freezes to my face before i can run very far, so I get out my dogsled and my Huskies take me for a spin over the frozen Tundra.<P>All kidding aside, just put on a headband if your ears get too cold. What I do is stretch and do a couple of excercises (pushups, wallsits) before I go outside so I am already warmed up. If you're running, you won't get cold.<BR>I love the cold air on a morning. It's so fresh and crisp.||||reg||1
